  "zones": {
    "$comment": "Player zone fields read by spawn / fishing conditions -> the boss that makes the zone reachable in practice; vanilla zones not listed are reachable from the start. Abyss layers per the Calamity wiki: layer 2 chests need Skeletron, Scoria in layer 3 is minable after Golem, layer 4 is meant for post-Polterghast. Calamity's Sunken Sea, Sulphurous Sea and Brimstone Crag exist from world generation. SOTS's pyramid, abandoned village and planetarium are world-generation structures (their chests carry their own locks); SOTS's Phase biome is the world-generated Phaseglass sky island. Catalyst's ZoneBlight is Calamity Vanities' Astral Blight, an Astral variant (that mod is not installed, so it is never true in game). SOTS's Anomaly biome is the area around a wormhole, which opens once all seven gem locks in the (world-generated) Planetarium hold their gem — vanilla gems, so nothing gates it; its two enemies are tuned harder than that, raise this if they turn up too early. Stars Above's six subworlds are Cosmic Voyage destinations, each reached with a Stellaglyph of its own tier (tier 3 wants souls, so hardmode) — rather than guess which voyage is which tier, all six are pinned to the mod's first boss.",
